      "label": "OpenAPI Ingest",
      "excerpt": "A made-up API to test against. An OpenAPI 3.1 description in FastAPI's shape, @a",
      "text": "This should be saved in the JSON5 and api.spell",
      "by": "owenoak",
      "at": "2026-11-17T20:24:02.558Z",
      "status": "answered",
      "quote": "No real data in checked-in files",
      "offset": 1498,
      "edited": "2026-11-17T20:24:08.280Z",
      "replies": [
        {
          "by": "owenoak",
          "agent": "claude",
          "at": "2026-11-17T20:29:35.530Z",
          "html": "<p>Keeping real values out is now a setting of the place:  written in its <code>.api.json5</code> and said in its <code>.api.spell</code>, so every later ingest, update and check keeps to it, and the flags only set it (plan step 5, a note on <a href=\"#j249\">J249</a>).  The rows go under <code>~/.spell/</code> in <code>read-page</code>'s samples files (<a href=\"#j259\">J259</a>).  Its Spell words are new, so they wait on your pick:  <a href=\"#q55\">Q55</a>.</p>"
        }
      ],
      "done": {
