    "c4": {
      "anchor": "q60",
      "kind": "item",
      "label": "How is a collection's master switch said, an unindented line that turns an operation off for every job?",
      "excerpt": "How is a collection's master switch said, an unindented line that turns an operation off for every job?",
      "text": "Same syntax -- if it's in the collection, it is the master switch",
      "by": "owenoak",
      "at": "2026-11-17T23:37:10.616Z",
      "status": "answered",
      "replies": [
        {
          "by": "owenoak",
          "agent": "claude",
          "at": "2026-11-17T23:42:00.920Z",
          "html": "<p>Recorded on <a href=\"#q60\">Q60</a> as your option, and chosen:  the master switch is the same line, <code>enabled operations are ...</code> or <code>all operations are disabled</code>.  In the collection it's the switch for every job, and on the thing it narrows that type.</p>\n<epic-code title=\"a whole .api.spell file, English\" language=\"spell\"><pre>netbox is a web server at \"https://demo.netbox.dev\"\n\tits token comes from \"https://auth.acme.test/api-keys/{key id}/token\", made with the secret \"NETBOX_KEY\"\n\tjobs live at \"/api/jobs\"\n\t\tenabled operations are add, change, complete       &lt;- the master switch:  no deleting any job\n\tjob sessions live at \"/api/job-session\"\n\t\tall operations are disabled                        &lt;- read only, for every job session\n\tto complete a job is at \"/api/jobs/{id}/complete\"\n\na \"job\" is a thing\n\tit lives in netbox\n\tthis type is unverified\n\tenabled operations are add, complete               &lt;- narrows:  this type can't be changed either</pre></epic-code>\n<epic-code title=\"the same, Spanish\" language=\"spell\"><pre>netbox es un servidor web en \"https://demo.netbox.dev\"\n\tsu token viene de \"https://auth.acme.test/api-keys/{key id}/token\", hecho con el secreto \"NETBOX_KEY\"\n\tlos trabajos están en \"/api/jobs\"\n\t\toperaciones activas: añadir, cambiar, completar\n\tlas sesiones de trabajo están en \"/api/job-session\"\n\t\ttodas las operaciones están desactivadas\n\tpara completar un trabajo está en \"/api/jobs/{id}/complete\"\n\nun \"trabajo\" es una cosa\n\tvive en netbox\n\teste tipo está sin verificar\n\toperaciones activas: añadir, completar</pre></epic-code>\n<p>Where it sits:  the <code>live at</code> lines are already indented under the web server's line, so \"in the collection\" is one step further in, under its own <code>live at</code> line.  It isn't on the web server's own lines.  Your earlier \"unindented\" can't sit at the file's left edge, as a line there names no collection.  So I've built it as above, and asked to be sure:  <a href=\"#q63\">Q63</a>.</p>\n<p>The switch wins:  the thing can only narrow it, and a thing listing <code>delete</code> when the switch leaves it out warns when it compiles.</p>"
        },
        {
          "by": "owenoak",
          "at": "2026-11-17T23:42:41.557Z",
          "text": "The"
        },
        {
          "by": "owenoak",
          "agent": "claude",
          "at": "2026-11-17T23:46:15.386Z",
          "html": "<p>Your reply here reads only \"The\": it looks cut off. Add the rest when you are ready.</p><p>Meanwhile Q63 is answered: the master switch sits one step in, under the collection's live at line, which is how P49 already has it.</p>"
        }
      ],
      "claim": {
